FramePack: encode each frame once, and stop carrying frames already written.

Both entry points call save_bcthw_as_mp4(history_pixels, ...) inside the section loop,
so section k re-encodes every frame produced so far: S(S+1)/2 sections' worth of frames
for an S-section run, plus one MP4 left on disk per section. The sampling loop is
constant-cost per section; this made a run quadratic in its own length.

demo_gradio_f1.py generates forward, so frames go to one open encoder as soon as
blending can no longer change them, and are then dropped from history_pixels. Output
is frame-for-frame identical and peak pixel memory becomes constant. The file is
fragmented per frame so the per-section preview stays playable while it is written.
demo_gradio.py generates in reverse, so each section's settled frames are encoded to
their own chunk and the chunks are joined by copying packets, never re-encoding.

Generated by fix_framepack.py.

